# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private CV data — NEVER commit. See CLAUDE.md, "Privacy".
#
# The site is statically generated and this repo is public, so anything tracked
# here is published permanently. Street address, phone, date of birth and the
# personal email live only in cv.private.yml, which Nuxt never reads — only
# scripts/build-cv.ts does, and only when passed --private.
#
# `npm run privacy:check` fails if any value from that file reaches a tracked
# file or the build output. It does NOT scan git history: by the time a value
# is committed it is already in every clone, which is why the check runs first
# in .githooks/pre-commit rather than anywhere later.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cv.private.yml
*.private.*
cv-out/
